🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- an out-of-bounds index into a struct array
🚽 field must be rejected (calculate_array_offset(), ast.c, reused as-is
🚽 from the array-variable path), not silently read/write past the
🚽 field's own bytes into a struct neighbor or off the end of the blob.
gang Foo {
    rizz arr[3];
};

skibidi main {
    gang Foo f;
    f.arr[5] = 1;
}
